74. šar₂ ki-sikil li-li ŋa₂-ŋa₂-de₃
#lem: šar[numerous]V/i; kisikil[young woman]; lilia[offspring]; ŋar[put]
#tr.en: To create offspring for thousands of young women, to make things in order like a potter, to cut the umbilical cord, to determine destinies, to place a hand on the door of the Niŋin-ŋar @noteref{a part of Ninisina's temple at Isin}, ……, to let the human child scream loud and long after it is received in the embrace, to turn its belly downwards and to turn it upside down, to …… the office of Mistress, to treat it quickly, to wash …… -- after she has made all these great divine powers appear gloriously, and my lady has spoken praise …… in addition, @wDN{Ninisina} praises herself fittingly: 
#etcsl: line-id=74

